      "gap": "Grinstead and Snell Definition 1.4 (sec. 1.2, book p. 28) defines the odds in favour of E as r : s with r/s = p/(1 - p) and adds the converse clause that, when r and s are given, p is found from p = r/(r + s); the text before it states that r to s odds mean the same as r/s to 1, so only the ratio matters (Example 1.12: 1/5 : 4/5 = 1 : 4 = 2 : 8). def:p15-finite-hypothesis-partition gives only the ratio P(G)/(1 - P(G)); the r : s representation and the converse formula p = r/(r + s) recovering the probability from given odds are not stated on the route.",
